menu "BLE CLI"

    config BLE_CLI_TX_QUEUE_DEPTH
        int "Response lines buffered for transmission"
        range 4 16
        default 8
        help
            REQ-PERF-04. Depth of the static TX queue (each item holds one whole
            response line of up to 128 bytes, about 136 bytes of .bss per slot).

    config BLE_CLI_CMD_QUEUE_DEPTH
        int "Parsed commands buffered for the worker"
        range 2 8
        default 4
        help
            Items are 12-byte parse results, not text. A burst beyond this depth
            sets the input-overflow latch and yields one ERR busy
            reason=input_overflow (tech_spec.md 2.5.2).

    config BLE_CLI_WORKER_STACK
        int "CLI worker task stack (bytes)"
        default 4096
        help
            REQ-MEM-04. Initial value; resize from the measured STACK_HWM.
            Allocated on the heap once at init.

    config BLE_CLI_WORKER_PRIO
        int "CLI worker task priority"
        range 1 10
        default 3
        help
            Below the accel session task (4), above the REPL (2).

    config BLE_CLI_DEBUG_TX_LOG
        bool "Log BLECLI_TX / BLECLI_TX_SUPPRESS lines (debug builds only)"
        default n
        help
            REQ-FUNC-61 verification aid: one line per transmitted or suppressed
            response line, with its length only, never its content (REQ-SEC-04).
            Leave n in production builds (test/configs/debug_tx.defaults sets it
            for the test image).

endmenu
